              "correctAnswer": "Form a small, real image of a distant object.",
              "explanation": "The large objective lens in a telescope is primarily a light-gathering element that collects light from a distant object and forms a small, real, inverted image at its focal plane. The eyepiece then acts as a magnifier to view this intermediate image."
